2:T523,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"The $13.8 Billion Awakening: China's Embodied AI Sector Hits Escape Velocity","description":"In the first half of 2026, China's embodied AI sector attracted $13.8 billion across 322 deals—a fivefold increase from a year ago. With Unitree Robotics clearing its STAR Market IPO in a record 104 days, Momenta listing as the 'physical AI first stock' at 414x oversubscription, and 22 unicorns now roaming the landscape, China's robotics industry has shifted from laboratory curiosity to capital market heavyweight.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523961131990-5ea7c61b2107?w=1200&h=600&fit=crop","datePublished":"2026-07-16T16:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-07-16T16:00:00.000Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Meeeeed@AI in China","url":"https://www.ainchina.com/about/"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI in China","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.ainchina.com/logo.svg"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.ainchina.com/blog/china-embodied-ai-13-billion-funding-boom-2026/"},"keywords":"[\"embodied AI\", \"humanoid robot\", \"Unitree IPO\", \"Momenta listing\", \"China robotics funding\", \"AI unicorn\", \"STAR Market\", \"physical AI\", \"Tesla Optimus\", \"ZhiPu\"]"}5:["slug","china-embodied-ai-13-billion-funding-boom-2026","d"]
0:["n8V4HI3bdOAeSri5wnB7-",[[["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","china-embodied-ai-13-billion-funding-boom-2026","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"china-embodied-ai-13-billion-funding-boom-2026\"}",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","china-embodied-ai-13-billion-funding-boom-2026","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"minHeight":"100vh","backgroundColor":"#0a0a0a","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","nav",null,{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"16px 24px"},"children":["$","div",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"1200px","margin":"0 auto","display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"24px"},"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/","style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","textDecoration":"none","fontWeight":"700","fontSize":"18px"},"children":"AI in China"}],["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/blog/","style":{"color":"#a3a3a3","textDecoration":"none","fontSize":"14px"},"children":"Blog"}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"800px","margin":"0 auto","padding":"48px 24px"},"children":[["$","header",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"48px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","gap":"12px","marginBottom":"24px","flexWrap":"wrap"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"0.05em"},"children":"AI Industry"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","color":"#737373"},"children":"16 min read"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"36px","fontWeight":"700","lineHeight":"1.2","margin":"0 0 24px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":"The $13.8 Billion Awakening: China's Embodied AI Sector Hits Escape Velocity"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"16px","color":"#737373","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"July 17, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"AI in China"}]]}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523961131990-5ea7c61b2107?w=1200&h=600&fit=crop","alt":"The $13.8 Billion Awakening: China's Embodied AI Sector Hits Escape Velocity","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","borderRadius":"12px","marginBottom":"48px"}}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","3",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*China's embodied AI sector has shifted from laboratory curiosity to capital market heavyweight in 2026. Photo: Unsplash*"}]]}],["$","h2","5",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Numbers That Changed Everything"}]]}],["$","p","7",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Something fundamental shifted in China's technology landscape between January and June 2026. According to data compiled by ITJuzi.Com, a Chinese investment intelligence platform, the country's embodied artificial intelligence sector attracted CNY 93.5 billion—approximately USD 13.8 billion—of financing in the first half of the year. That represents a fivefold jump from the same period in 2025. The deal count was equally staggering: 322 financing transactions, more than double the 150 or so recorded a year earlier."}]]}],["$","p","9",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"To put this in perspective, China's entire embodied AI sector raised roughly what a single major American AI lab might spend on training a frontier model in 2026. But unlike pure software plays, this capital is being deployed into physical hardware—motors, sensors, actuators, manufacturing facilities, and the \"brains\" that will eventually control millions of robots."}]]}],["$","p","11",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The capital concentration tells its own story. Funding has clustered around three pillars: the research and development of embodied AI large language models, the large-scale collection of robot training data, and product delivery capabilities. In other words, investors are no longer writing checks based on demo videos or conference presentations. They are betting on companies that can ship."}]]}],["$","div","21",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Metric"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"H1 2026"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"H1 2025"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Change"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Total Funding (USD)"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"$$13.8 billion"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~$2.8 billion"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+393%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Deal Count"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"322"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~150"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+115%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"New Unicorns"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"19"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+533%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Companies in IPO Pipeline"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"19"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"4"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+375%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"HK Listings (H1)"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"10"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+400%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"A-Share IPO Filings"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"1"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+200%"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p","22",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Key Insight:"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" The deal velocity and capital deployment suggest 2026 is the inflection point where China's embodied AI industry transitions from \"science project\" to \"industrial scale.\""}]]}],["$","h2","24",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Unitree's Lightning IPO: From Lab Bench to STAR Market in 104 Days"}]]}],["$","p","26",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"On July 1, 2026, the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) issued a registration approval for Unitree Robotics' initial public offering on Shanghai's STAR Market—the Nasdaq-style board designed for high-tech companies. The approval came just 104 days after the IPO application was accepted on March 20, making it the fastest review process in STAR Market history under the pre-review mechanism. Unitree passed its listing hearing in 73 days, surpassing the previous record held by Moore Threads at 88 days."}]]}],["$","p","28",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Unitree plans to raise CNY 4.202 billion (approximately $620 million) to expand production of humanoid robots, strengthen embodied AI research and development, and build new manufacturing facilities. At least 10 percent of the company's shares will be offered in the IPO."}]]}],["$","p","30",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The financials underpinning this valuation are instructive. Unitree reported annual revenue of CNY 1.7 billion in 2025 with a net profit of CNY 280 million—a remarkable turnaround from net losses of CNY 22.1 million in 2022 and CNY 11.15 million in 2023. In the first quarter of 2026, revenue surged to CNY 420 million, up 68.5 percent year-on-year, though net profit fell 47.7 percent to CNY 50 million as the company increased spending on expansion."}]]}],["$","p","32",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"According to the 2025 humanoid robot market research report released by CCID Media, China had more than 140 humanoid robot manufacturers in 2025, with total shipments reaching 14,400 units. Unitree alone accounted for 84.7 percent of the global market. The Ministry of Industry and Information Technology said Chinese humanoid robot manufacturers had launched over 330 product models by the end of 2025."}]]}],["$","p","34",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Unitree's overseas push has already begun. Co-developed humanoid robots recently entered Tokyo's Haneda Airport for trial operations launched by Japan Airlines, testing ground handling operations including baggage loading and unloading, cargo transport, and conveyor coordination. The trials are scheduled to continue through 2028—described by the company as the first commercial application of a Chinese humanoid robot inside a major global aviation hub."}]]}],["$","div","43",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Year"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Revenue (CNY M)"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Net Profit (CNY M)"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Key Milestone"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2022"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"—"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"-22.1"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Founded 2016, quadruped focus"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2023"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"—"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"-11.15"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Expanded into humanoids"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2024"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"—"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+94.5"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"First profitable year"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2025"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"1,700"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+280"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Spring Festival Gala performance"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Q1 2026"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"420"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"+50"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Revenue +68.5% YoY, profit -47.7%"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","img","44",{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581091226825-a6a2a5aee158?w=800&q=80","alt":"Advanced robotics manufacturing and assembly line","style":{"width":"100%","borderRadius":"12px","margin":"24px 0"}}],["$","p","45",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*China's robotics manufacturers are scaling from prototype to production at unprecedented speed. Photo: Unsplash*"}]]}],["$","h2","47",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Momenta's Wall of Money: The \"Physical AI First Stock\" Rewrites Hong Kong"}]]}],["$","p","49",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"If Unitree's IPO represents the establishment of a domestic A-share pathway for robotics companies, Momenta's listing on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on July 8, 2026, represents the global capital markets' validation of China's physical AI thesis."}]]}],["$","p","51",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Momenta priced its shares at HKD 295.6 and saw its public offering oversubscribed by 414 times—an extraordinary vote of confidence from international investors. The company raised approximately HKD 6.8 billion, and its market capitalization surpassed HKD 700 billion on its first trading day, with the stock climbing more than 6 percent intraday."}]]}],["$","p","53",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Momenta is widely regarded as the \"physical AI first stock\" (物理AI第一股), a label that captures the investor narrative: this is not merely an autonomous driving company, but a physical AI platform whose technology stack—perception, reasoning, and real-world interaction—can be generalized across robotics applications."}]]}],["$","p","55",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The listing's success signals that international long-term capital is willing to price Chinese physical AI companies at premium valuations, provided the technology narrative is compelling and the path to commercialization is credible. For the broader embodied AI sector, Momenta's valuation sets a benchmark that other IPO candidates will now be measured against."}]]}],["$","h2","57",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Unicorn Factory: 22 Startups, $20 Billion Valuations, and Counting"}]]}],["$","p","59",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The rapid pace of fundraising has created a unicorn stampede. Unitree Robotics, AgiBot, and Galbot achieved valuations exceeding CNY 10 billion (approximately $1.47 billion) each in 2025, becoming the early embodied AI unicorns. In 2026, they have been joined by another 19 firms, including Deep Robotics, X Square Robot, AI² Robotics, Galaxea AI, and Spirit AI."}]]}],["$","p","61",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Among the newer cohort, four companies have already surpassed CNY 20 billion in valuation: Galbot, X Square Robot, AI² Robotics, and Galaxea AI. This concentration of value in the upper tier suggests investors are making calculated bets on category leaders rather than spreading capital evenly across the field."}]]}],["$","p","63",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The investor roster is equally notable. HongShan, the rebranded Sequoia Capital China, participated in 20 financing rounds involving 14 companies in the first half of 2026. GL Ventures, the early-stage affiliate of Hillhouse Capital, took part in 18 rounds across 14 companies. The National Artificial Intelligence Industry Investment Fund—a state-backed vehicle—has invested in companies including Galbot and Deep Robotics, while local government-backed investors such as Shenzhen Capital Group have funded at least 12 companies. Automotive giants SAIC Motor and BAIC Group Industrial Investment have also entered the sector."}]]}],["$","p","65",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This mix of venture capital, state funds, and industrial strategic investors creates a capital ecosystem that is arguably deeper and more diversified than what exists for American robotics startups."}]]}],["$","div","76",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Company"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Focus"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Valuation (CNY B)"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Valuation (USD B)"}]]}],["$","th","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Key Investors"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Unitree Robotics"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Humanoid robots"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"sty