al-scene training (实景实训专项行动), requiring key scenario deployments by the end of the year."}]]}],["$","p","113",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The data infrastructure is equally critical. China has established 27 data-collection sites nationwide to support the training of embodied AI systems. These sites provide the physical environments—warehouses, factories, airports, hospitals—where robots can learn through interaction rather than simulation."}]]}],["$","p","115",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Local government competition has intensified. Shenzhen, Hangzhou, Beijing, and Shanghai have all announced robotics industry development plans, with subsidies, tax incentives, and dedicated industrial parks. The National Artificial Intelligence Industry Investment Fund has directly backed multiple embodied AI companies, signaling that the sector is viewed as strategically important at the highest levels of industrial policy."}]]}],["$","p","117",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Roland Berger forecasts that more than 30 robot and core component makers will go public by the end of 2026, potentially driving up the industry's overall valuation significantly. The consulting firm sees the sector transitioning from a \"capital-driven phase\" to an \"industry competition phase.\""}]]}],["$","div","127",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Policy/Initiative"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Authority"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Timeline"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Impact"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Real-scene training special action"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"MIIT + SASAC"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2026"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Mandatory deployment in key scenarios"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"27 national data collection sites"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"National program"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Ongoing"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children"