venue alongside widening losses creates a \"scissors gap\" that public market investors may not tolerate indefinitely."}]]}],["$","p","135",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The IPO pipeline itself is a source of both strength and vulnerability. Nineteen companies have initiated the listing process, but only three—Unitree, Deep Robotics, and Leju—have submitted prospectuses to regulators. The remaining 16 are in earlier stages of preparation, and their ability to meet public market standards for revenue growth, corporate governance, and financial transparency remains unproven."}]]}],["$","p","137",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Valuations in the private market are driven by technological expectations and industry growth potential. Once in the public market, companies must substantiate those valuations through revenue growth, product delivery, customer acquisition, and commercialization capabilities. The transition from private to public pricing will be a stern test for many."}]]}],["$","p","139",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Industry analysts also caution that the global humanoid robot market remains nascent. Morgan Stanley and Nomura have predicted 2026 China shipments of 50,000 to 62,500 units—impressive growth, but still a fraction of the millions of units that would justify the current aggregate valuation of the sector."}]]}],["$","div","147",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Risk Factor"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Severity"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Mitigation"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Timeline"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Profitability gap"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"High"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Scale manufacturing, reduce BOM"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"12-18 months"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"IPO pipeline quality"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Medium"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Regulatory scrutiny, restructuring"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"6-12 months"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Valuation compression"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Medium"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Revenue growth, delivery proof"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3-6 months"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Market size uncertainty"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Low"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Policy mandates, industrial demand"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Ongoing"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","h2","148",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"What to Watch in Q3 and Q4 2026"}]]}],["$","p","150",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The second half of 2026 will bring several critical milestones that will determine whether the first-half momentum is sustainable or speculative."}]]}],["$","p","152",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"First, Unitree's actual IPO pricing and post-listing performance will set the tone for the A-share robotics cohort. If the stock trades well, the STAR Market could become the preferred venue for domestic robotics listings; if it underperforms, the Hong Kong pathway favored by AgiBot, Galbot, and others will look more attractive."}]]}],["$","p","154",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Second, Tesla's Optimus production ramp in Fremont will provide a direct comparison point. If Tesla achieves its 1,000-unit weekly target by September, the competitive pressure on Chinese manufacturers will intensify. If the ramp is delayed, Chinese companies will have additional breathing room to consolidate their domestic market share."}]]}],["$","p","156",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Third, the delivery numbers from UBTECH, ZhiYuan, and other volume producers will reveal whether the pre-order figures translate into actual shipments. The gap between \"orders\" and \"delivered units\" has historically been wide in robotics, and 2026 will be the year that gap either narrows or exposes the sector's commercialization challenges."}]]}],["$","p","158",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Fourth, ZhiPu's HKD 31.4 billion placement—completed on July 9, 2026—signals that the \"brain\" layer of embodied AI is attracting capital at unprecedented scale. How ZhiPu deploys that capital into physical AI applications will be closely watched."}]]}],["$","div","168",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,